cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or dataset, please cite the accompanying manuscript and this repository."
title: "Vagus Nerve Atlas Explorer: a standardized map of human vagus nerve branch emergence"
abstract: >
  Interactive browser-based atlas and reproducibility companion for the
  manuscript "A standardized map of human vagus nerve branch emergence
  defines anatomical targets for function-selective neuromodulation".
  The explorer exposes a registered, landmark-anchored cohort of 28
  human vagus nerves (56 nerves, 2,177 branches) through filters for
  donor, side, sex, supergroup, and subgroup, with four coupled
  visualization panels (Individual Branches, Subway Map, Distributions,
  Selectivity) and a reproducibility notebook that regenerates every
  figure and table in the manuscript from the same dataset the explorer
  reads.
type: software
license: MIT
